                <pb facs="0744" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg624"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Great Britain/288: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain (Mellon) to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-05-03T18:00:00+01:00">May 3, 1932—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 3—1:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>161. With reference to my telegram 155, April 29, noon,<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d421-f1"/> I have received the following note from Vansittart today. Kindly give copy to
                        Ogden Mills.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“It is the intention of His Majesty’s Government in the United Kingdom to
                        designate His Majesty’s Ambassador in Washington to confer with the United
                        States Government with a view to signature of the proposed agreement. We
                        hope to be in a position to send Sir Ronald
                            Lindsay the necessary instructions at an early date.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mellon</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
